@startuml single-signal-path
title US-06: Single Signal Path - Only One Weak Signal Present, No Composite Raised

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

participant "Alert\nEvaluator\n(leader)" as Evaluator
database "Redis\nalert-state:{id}" as AlertState
queue "Kafka\nproximity.candidates" as ProxKafka
queue "Kafka\nalerts" as Kafka

== Signal loss only - no proximity candidate arrives ==

note over Evaluator
  Signal loss detected via scheduled Redis scan.
  alert-state:VesselB set. SIGNAL_LOSS alert emitted.
  No proximity.candidates event has arrived
  for VesselB within the loss window.
  Only one weak signal present.
  No composite alert raised.
end note

Evaluator -> Kafka : publish individual SIGNAL_LOSS alert\n{ alert_id, alert_type: SIGNAL_LOSS, entity_id: VesselB }

== Proximity candidate arrives - no active signal loss ==

ProxKafka -> Evaluator : consume proximity.candidates event\n{ entity_a_id: VesselC, entity_b_id: VesselD,\n  timestamp_ms, lat, lon, distance_metres }

Evaluator -> AlertState : GET alert-state:VesselC
AlertState --> Evaluator : nil - no active signal loss for VesselC

Evaluator -> AlertState : GET alert-state:VesselD
AlertState --> Evaluator : nil - no active signal loss for VesselD

note over Evaluator
  VesselC and VesselD are in proximity
  but neither has gone dark.
  No signal loss component.
  Only one weak signal present.
  No composite alert raised.
end note

Evaluator -> Kafka : publish individual UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY alert\n{ alert_id, alert_type: UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY,\n  entity_c, entity_d }

note over Kafka
  Composite alert requires BOTH:
  signal loss AND proximity to an
  unrelated entity within the loss window.
  Neither case above qualifies.
end note

@enduml
